\ulnone\cf2 Kadakol-HaveriB Upendran | HENB | Bengaluru | Nov 1, 2024:: Around 200 police personnel and four KSRP platoons have been rushed to Kadakol when tension erupted in Kadakol village, Haveri district. After fearing Waqf Board's takeover of their properties, Hindu villagers attacked Muslim's buildings, injuring five. Police restored peace, detained 32 for investigation. Karnataka Waqf minister B Z Zameer Ahmed Khan blamed BJP for misleading farmers as verification of Waqf property claims is underway. BJP vehemently protested the Karanataka Govt's conspiracy to grab the lands of Hindu farmers with the tool of draconian Waqf provisions.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Tensions flared up in Kadakol village, Karnataka's Haveri district, on Wednesday night, due to a government notice about the Waqf Board claiming ownership of homes sparked violence. Fearing loss of property, Hindu villagers, mainly of farmer folks, targeted Muslim community, damaging their homes, property, and a motorcycle, and injuring five people. The situation escalated, leaving one person critically injured and hospitalized in stable condition at KIMS Hospital in Hubballi.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
